.TH MERIDIAN-CALENDAR 1 "September 2026" "Meridian 1.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
meridian-calendar \- a calm, private calendar for the desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B meridian-calendar
[\fIOPTION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Meridian is a calendar with day, week, month and agenda views, repeating
events, reminders and colour-coded calendars. All data stays on this
computer; Meridian never connects to the network.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-new\-event
Open Meridian ready to add a new event. If Meridian is already running,
the request is sent to the running instance.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-background
Start without opening a window. Reminders are still delivered.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable the web inspector and print page console messages.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/meridian/calendar.json
Calendars and events.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/meridian/backups/
Rolling daily backups (the last seven days).
.TP
.I ~/.config/meridian/settings.json
Preferences.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MERIDIAN_DATA_DIR
Use this folder for data and settings instead of the defaults.
.SH SEE ALSO
Press Ctrl+? inside Meridian for keyboard shortcuts.
